This directory must exist in the repository even though its real contents
are gitignored — see docs/DEPENDENCY_BUNDLING_PLAN.md's Implementation log.

tauri-build validates that every `bundle.resources` path in tauri.conf.json
exists on EVERY cargo invocation (`cargo check`/`test`/`clippy`/`build`), not
only when actually bundling via `tauri build`. A fully gitignored directory
here broke plain `cargo check` for every contributor and CI job that hasn't
run `node scripts/fetch-ollama-runtime.mjs` first (a real CI failure, not a
hypothetical one — see the "Rust Tests & Clippy" job).

Run `node scripts/fetch-ollama-runtime.mjs <platform>` to populate this
directory with the real, checksum-verified Ollama runtime before running
`tauri build`. Do not commit that fetched content — only this placeholder.
